@startuml pattern-selection-guide
!include pattern-theme.puml

title Pattern Selection Guide\n<size:14>Start with the simplest orchestration model that matches the problem</size>

note as guide #FFFFFF
|= Situation |= Recommended pattern |= Coordination model |
| Fixed stages with dependent outputs | **Sequential** | Ordered chain |
| Several independent perspectives | **Parallel** | Fan-out / fan-in |
| Same operation over many items | **Parallel Mapper** | Concurrent map-reduce |
| Quality requires repeated refinement | **Loop** | Exit-condition cycle |
| Input determines the specialist | **Conditional** | Runtime branch |
| Task decomposition is not known upfront | **Supervisor** | LLM planning + delegation |
| Approval or missing context needs a person | **Human-in-the-Loop** | Human gate |
| Goal has data dependencies | **GOAP** | Shortest dependency path |
| Peers should react to shared state | **P2P** | Decentralized collaboration |
| Strong opposing arguments matter | **Debate** | Multi-round adversarial panel |
| Independent categorical judgments matter | **Voting** | Ensemble majority |
end note

@enduml